MPL-2.0 — Mozilla Public License 2.0
================================================================================

The following crates are licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0:
  https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/

  cssparser     — Servo project, Mozilla
  selectors     — Servo project, Mozilla

MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft license. HTMLCut carries the `selectors`
source under `patches/rust/selectors/` so the downstream-safe selector stack
travels with `htmlcut-core`; the vendored copy keeps the upstream MPL-2.0
license. HTMLCut also carries selector work accounting and parser-diagnostic adaptations,
and rewires dependencies onto paired local crates.
The MPL-2.0 license text and source are available at
https://github.com/servo/servo and the corresponding crates.io pages.

================================================================================
Local patched dependencies — selector and parser safety
================================================================================

HTMLCut carries a vendored downstream-safe selector/parser stack under:

  patches/rust/scraper
  patches/rust/selectors
  patches/rust/html5ever
  patches/rust/markup5ever
  patches/rust/servo_arc
  patches/rust/tendril

These local copies exist so git/path consumers of `htmlcut-core` inherit the
same strict-provenance fixes that HTMLCut verifies under Miri. Their upstream
licenses remain unchanged:

  scraper                           — ISC
  selectors                         — MPL-2.0
  html5ever, markup5ever,
  servo_arc, tendril                — MIT OR Apache-2.0

Patch provenance, verification, and removal cues live in `patches/README.md`.

